Byron A Jeff wrote:
> I have a pre-quest Monk with the following stats:
> This is the first Monk I've taken this deep into midgame. So here's my
> dilimma:  g - a wand of wishing (0:1)
>
> Of course a wish could go to a Helm of Brilliance. Monks can
> get to decent spellcasting abilities, and I can definitely see a
> HoB/robe combo as useful as I progress deeper into the game.
>
> One site suggests that The Eye of the Aethiopica may be a good choice
> because it confers MR when carried, so it can substitute for GDSM
> which are virtually useless for Monks.

The Eye should be your #1 priority.  Without some non-wielded
not-your-own-Quest artifact source of MR (or GDSM/scales, which is
problematic for low/mid-level monks), you can't safely wear a robe
(wielded weapons are not safe in the face of bullwhips, among other
things).

But it's the other features that set it apart.  Mana regeneration +
portals are incredibly useful, and even without MR there's a good case
to be made that it's the most powerful item in the game other than a
/wishing.

As long as you stay at enough hp (20) to survive the blast, it will
airlift you to safety instantaneously.  Mana regen lets you blast
attack spells with impunity, and more importantly lets you cast magic
mapping/clairvoyance in gehennom.

IOW, the Eye is far more important to a would-be caster than the
HoBrilliance, especially to someone wearing a robe.

The helm is reasonable though personally I rarely find it worth a wish;
a decent elvish leather helm (one that you find at +2 or +3) is usually
my helm of choice unless I randomly find a helm of brilliance before I
start enchanting things.

You mention boots.  I'd go w/ jumping boots, but if you aren't going to
remember to use them speed boots are better.  Either one is a solid
choice.  Other than that, conflict would be at the top of my list,
followed by _maybe_ =teleport control (or c?genocide to get wraiths to
level up to where you get intrinsic TC).

With the markers you have, better AC should be easy to get.  Given your
circumstances, wishing for ?EA is not unreasonable if you haven't
identified them yet (your entire focus is to survive long enough to get
the castle wand; since you'll have a full AK by then the castle wand
will have all the "reserve" wishes you need), obviously if you have
then use your markers to get that AC in the -25 range and wish for
another marker instead of ?EA if you need them.

Either ?earth+telecontrol or jumping boots alone will let you take out
Master Kaen with no real risk.



